   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend a chapter of the laws of 2019, relating to directing the study\nof the future implementation of fifth and future generation wireless network\nsystem technology in the state, in relation to the agencies which shall\nconduct such study",
    "basePrintNo": "S7179",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7179-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1, 2 & 3, Chap of 2019 (as proposed in S.1607 & A.1503)",
    "lawSection": "State Technology",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7179\n\nSPONSOR: PARKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend a chapter of the laws of 2019, relating to directing the\nstudy of the future implementation of fifth and future generation wire-\nless network system technology in the state, in relation to the agencies\nwhich shall conduct such study\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2019,\nc.653.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis chapter amendment adds the department of public service, the urban\ndevelopment corporation, the division of homeland security and energy\nservices, the division of state police and the division of military and\nnaval affairs, as state agencies to the bill that will study and prepare\na report on 5g technology.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe five agencies were added to ensure the report was developed by agen-\ncies with legal jurisdiction over parties and issues related to cyberse-\ncurity, telecommunications, wireless networks, and related infrastruc-\nture.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nN/A\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2019, relating to directing the study of the\nfuture implementation of fifth and future generation wireless network\nsystem technology in the state, as proposed in legislative bills numbers\nS. 1607 and A. 1503, takes effect.\n",
